      "claim": "Signed favorable-minus-comparison endpoint contrasts are strongest and most reproducible for the short-range pair kernels: pair_kernel_1.5 (integrated z 0.562, q 1.5e-4, positive batch fraction 1.0), pair_kernel_2.5 (0.631, q 2.2e-5, 1.0) and pair_kernel_3.5 (0.540, q 9.8e-5, 1.0), with pair_kernel_5.0 weaker (0.319, q 3.7e-3) and pair_kernel_7.0 negative (-0.485, q 1.5e-4, positive batch fraction 0.0). The same ordering appears in the branch-adjusted raw and adjusted correlations (pair_kernel_1.5 and 2.5 positive with q<0.02; pair_kernel_7.0 negative). These are selection/endpoint enrichment contrasts on a radial pair-distance shell density, not interaction energies or absolute geometric targets.",
